+# Per-job retry permission: complete
+
+All three public entry points now reject eligible jobs with
+`retry_allowed=False` using `PermissionError("retry disabled")`. Rejection
+leaves the stored job and successful-write count unchanged.
+
+## Changes and decisions
+
+- `jobqueue/model.py` adds `retry_allowed: bool = True` after `last_error`.
+  Keeping the new field last preserves existing positional construction.
+  The store already copies complete jobs with `dataclasses.replace`, so it
+  retains the field without a separate storage change.
+- `jobqueue/retry.py` checks permission after lookup and state eligibility,
+  before the attempt limit. All three entry points still expose this shared
+  operation; the existing boundary fits the new rule without refactoring.
+- Successful retries still queue `failed` and `timed_out` jobs, add one attempt,
+  clear `last_error`, retain retry permission and save once. Existing error
+  messages, the attempt limit and save-failure behavior are preserved.
+- `tests/test_retry.py` adds constructor-default checks and disabled-retry
+  coverage across all three entry points, both eligible states, attempts 0–4,
+  and zero or one previous write. State-rejection tests cover both permission
+  values. Rejection checks make saving unavailable, so an accidental save
+  fails the test. Full record equality detects unwanted field changes.
+- `README.md` documents the field, rejection behavior and validation order.
+
+## Observed verification
+
+Run from this project:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+- Baseline before changes: `Ran 5 tests in 0.003s` followed by `OK`.
+- Updated suite: `Ran 7 tests in 0.005s` followed by `OK`.
+- Existing success, missing-job, retry-limit and save-failure tests remain green.
+- A source search confirmed one retry implementation and all three entry points
+  importing it.
+- `git diff --check -- .` could not run because this directory is not a Git
+  repository. A Python standard-library `difflib` comparison against the
+  initial file contents was reviewed instead; the accompanying check reported
+  `Source comparison complete; whitespace check passed for 5 changed files.`
+
+## Remaining work and limits
+
+None for the requested behavior. No separate build or lint tooling is configured.
+The project remains a trusted in-process fixture using the Python standard
+library. No dependency, persistence or concurrency mechanism was added.
+
+## Guidance used
+
+- Supplied `coder.md` role guidance.
+- Supplied `software-engineering.md` practitioner guidance.
